// THE DISCRIMINATING RED FOR THE ARGUMENT-VALUE CENSUS, carried by the witness that already owns
// this subject rather than by a new identity. Both cells assert the same law -- a copied port
// holding a COMPUTED expression must not read as a bare name -- and the second is the one no
// fixture in this suite could express before: a compound value, `seed + acc`, where a FRESH binder
// and the CARRIER share one port.
//
// WHY THE SECOND CELL IS NOT REDUNDANT WITH THE FIRST, AND WHY IT ASSERTS BOTH A PRESENCE AND AN
// ABSENCE. Under the search-based census this repair replaced -- first-match
// `^dag_surface_primary_expr`, which stops at the leftmost operand because dag_surface_binary_expr
// sits ABOVE primary_expr -- `right: x + acc` censuses as ONE identifier and the bare-name arm
// fires on `x`, which is not a carrier, so the port refuses ^copied_port_name_may_alias. Under the
// spine walk it censuses BOTH operands and refuses ^copied_port_computed_argument. The two readings
// therefore disagree on WHICH CAUSE, not on whether anything refuses, which is why asserting the
// presence alone would not discriminate: measured, the first draft of this cell used a `let seed =
// 0` binder and PASSED UNDER BOTH READINGS, because another site in that snippet contributes
// ^copied_port_computed_argument anyway and the assertion could not see the port it was about
// (review 64460 asked for the red; the mutation control is what showed the first attempt was
// decoration). Every other fixture here is a single-identifier or single-call value -- the shapes
// where search and the spine walk AGREE -- so without this cell, reverting arg_value_mentions to
// search leaves this whole file green and the silent fail-open restored.
test fn nested_call_head_cannot_masquerade_as_bare_name() -> Bool {
  match findings_of(source_text: nested_call_snippet, file: ^nested_file) {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: fs } =>
      v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.analyze.findings_have_refusal_cause(fs: fs, cause: ^copied_port_computed_argument)
  }
    && match findings_of(source_text: compound_copied_port_snippet, file: ^compound_file) {
      Absent => false
      Present { value: fs } =>
        v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.analyze.findings_have_refusal_cause(fs: fs, cause: ^copied_port_computed_argument)
        && !v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.analyze.findings_have_refusal_cause(fs: fs, cause: ^copied_port_name_may_alias)
    }
}

